 "details": {
  "title": "I’ll Get By",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet in B♭ (C for the trumpet), concert A3 to D5, about 84, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement and checked note by note against the page’s guide voice: the whole song, then the second half again, with a breath every four bars where a long note ends. A short line opens over the guitar’s E♭ major 7, E♭ minor 6 and the turn back, and it closes over B♭6 and E♭ minor 6 over B♭, G♭ falling to F. The song is from 1928, so it is free to use.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Fred E. Ahlert and Roy Turk (1928)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune as the Fret Finder page’s guide voice sings it, on that page’s chords"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "B♭ major concert (C for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, A B A C, the second half again, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (igb-guitar.mp3), 2:30"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The page numbers its four intro bars i1 to i4, so its bar 1 is bar 5 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
